      "note": "This is the portal's public sample key, so it is capped at five trains per line: what is drawn is a sample of the fleet, not the whole of it. The endpoint reports which station a train is at, never a position, so each train sits on its station's coordinate and a train at a station the table cannot resolve — or a name shared by two stations, such as 양평 — is not drawn at all. The sample key is limited to 1,000 requests a day for everyone together, so after the first poll only two lines are re-polled per minute and each keeps its last report for up to 15 minutes. Register a free key at data.seoul.go.kr and put it in `base` in place of `sample` for full coverage and no rotation. Korean buses and the metro of Busan, Daegu, Daejeon and Gwangju publish no keyless feed, so they are absent."
